    <!-- Setup sheet -->
    <string name="setup_title">Choose how hue-shift works</string>
    <string name="setup_intro">For security reasons Android does not let ordinary apps change the colours of other apps. hue-shift can do it in one of three ways:</string>
    <string name="setup_shizuku_steps">1. Install Shizuku and start it (via Wireless debugging on Android 11+, or with ADB from a computer).\n2. Come back here and tap “Grant access”.</string>
    <string name="setup_shizuku_reboot">After a phone restart Shizuku has to be started again. hue-shift then brings the filter back by itself.</string>
    <string name="setup_root_steps">Your root manager (Magisk, KernelSU, APatch…) will ask once for permission.</string>
    <string name="setup_overlay_steps">Turn on “hue-shift” in Settings → Accessibility. The service only draws the colour layer and never reads the screen.</string>
    <string name="setup_overlay_restricted">Switch greyed out? Open App info → ⋮ → “Allow restricted settings” (Android 13+, apps installed from a file).</string>
    <string name="setup_auto_hint">hue-shift picks the best ready mode automatically.</string>
    <string name="setup_system_colours_note">While a filter is on, it takes priority over Night Light and the system colour correction.</string>
